mantle rm322
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for cty_mogens_mudstack
title the borrowed kitchen rule
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=woodcutter
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk names_a_cut_by_an_imagined_grandmothers_kitchen_rule
likes hard_cheese long_walks sharp_knife misty_dawns
dislikes cold_tea stale_bread
fears an_unanswered_letter_turning_brittle
hopes to_learn_a_cut_that_needs_no_name
topics work +0.4 friends +0.3 food +0.3 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=warm gossip=chatty refuse=soft tease=warm
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# gives every odd piece of wood a kitchen use and invents an elderly critic to judge the workmanship.

words
oath! = Shave my best spoon | By the crooked ladle
saying! = A branch can have a second supper | Nobody stirs soup with a family tree
spoon = a spoon in waiting | my half-cut ladle
curl = a tight wood shaving | a pale curl of grain
hook = a wooden pot hook | a branch with a good elbow
sap = a spot of sap | a sticky tear of resin
knife = my keen little knife | a blade with a walnut grip
cheese = a corner of dense cheese | a knuckle of salt cheese
letter = my folded letter | the paper in my inside pocket
rack = a split-stick rack | a greenwood trivet
road = a long outwards path | my walking road
fog = a veil between stems | the morning mist
cup = a squat tea bowl | a clay cup
crumb = a stubborn crust | a dry hunk of bread

any
opinion dole for 1 : Plenty of spare hands for stirring a pot. Plenty of wolves who could use what comes up on the spoon too.
opinion festivals for 2 : At a dance it's my pleasure to spend hours displaying what a spoon handle looks like on legs.
opinion houses against 1 : I'd like one grand name to come stand beside a stump and see what the next year's warming really costs.
opinion merchants against 1 : One copper more on cheese is a great squeeze on the poor last mouthful.
opinion strangers for 1 : Show me somebody I've never fed and you've found the very wolf to share a cheese heel with.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You're welcome at the short end of the ladle. | Room for a fresh pair of opinions.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Come over my working shoulder. | Stand away from the flying curls and say your piece.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Day's barely peeled. Hello to you. | Morning with the bark still on it.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. It's all spoon-coloured light. | Come see what the day's whittled down to.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family needn't apply for a spoon. | Sit in among the familiar elbows.
line again.open : We cross handles again. | You've come back for my remaining half opinion.
line greet.return : There's a voice above the shavings. | Good, I heard the greeting clean.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Come closer, you know my splinter side. | Your voice rubs smooth in my ear.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Speak while the shaving's curling. | I'll put the keen edge down a moment.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I can see the grin from here. | Come up to where the light still works.
line farewell : Good wood under every step. | Walk till something crooked makes you smile.
line farewell.return : I'll keep the handle this end. | Fine grain along your road.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Find yourself a lamp with a generous wick. | Easy night beyond the last tree shadow.
line react.news : Let's hear the shape of it. | Put that chunk of news in my paw.
line react.news.new : Well, that's a fresh cut. | Haven't seen that grain before.
line react.news.known : I've had a shaving off that story already. | I know the curl on that account.
line react.news.doubt : I'd give that knot another good look first. | There's more bend in that account than wood.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Ah, that bites deeper than a sharp edge. | Let me carry something beside you.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good grain clean through that news. | I'd carve a smile to suit the occasion.
line ask.how : How's the old spoon handle sitting today? | Did the day leave your knuckles whole?
line answer.how : Still an elbow short of a perfect ladle. | Merrily taking the bark off my worries.
line decline : I reckon I've enough curls to clear just here. | Let me save the keen edge for my own wood.
line accept_decline : Your handle, your decision. | Good. I'll stop stirring.
line thank : A kindness worth a spoonful of cheese. | That eases a tight bit of grain.
line sympathise : Here's a broad shoulder for a crooked trouble. | Let me hold the weighty end awhile.
line reassure : Even a knot can come out handsome. | There's a good handle left in that branch.
line preclose : I'll go see which shavings have caught on me. | Time to fold my knife and move.

scene gran
when topic=work self.job=woodcutter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I run every branch past an imaginary kitchen judge.
b : Whose kitchen? | Hard to please?
a : My invented kitchen elder would look at a fine stick and see #hook#. | Oh yes. I invented the judge but seldom get an easy hearing.

scene split
when topic=work self.job=woodcutter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A branch with an elbow makes a better hook than a straight branch persuaded otherwise.
b : Why keep the elbow? | For a heavy pot?
a : The grain turned the corner before my knife ever touched it. | If the grain's sound. I test it low down before entrusting a supper to it.

scene edge
when topic=pastimes self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My knife should take #curl# with no more than finger pressure.
b : Why so fine? | How can you tell?
a : Fine curls start a fire and save my wrist a quarrel. | The wood shines where the cut passed without tearing.

scene cheese
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut cheese into little roof tiles.
b : Does it taste different? | For a cheese house?
a : It lasts longer, which improves the last piece wonderfully. | The roof disappears tile by tile while I'm planning the walls.

scene walk
when topic=travel self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The finest walk takes me far enough to forget whose errand I might have been on.
b : You walk back too? | How far is that?
a : Naturally. Supper can't be expected to follow my footprints. | A little past the point where my list of duties runs out of breath.

scene tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cold tea has the colour of a fine wood stain and approximately the same charm in a cup.
b : Would you stain a spoon? | Would you still drink it?
a : An old handle maybe. I'd keep the tea off the business end. | Only if the pot was emptier than my patience.

scene crumb
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dislike a crust old enough to take a good polish.
b : Can you soften it? | Has it any use?
a : A hearty stew deals with bread better than a keen blade does. | I never saw a piece I couldn't put to work holding a bit of cheese.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In mist a coppice starts by showing only the nearest elbows.
b : Of the trees? | Is the path visible?
a : Trees first, my own second. I'm careful with both. | Enough to enjoy discovering the next bit twice as I walk.

scene forgot
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have a letter so soft at the folds it scarcely makes a rustle.
b : A good letter? | Will you read it again?
a : Dear enough to keep. I won't invite the whole street to read it. | Possibly. Waiting for an answer doesn't need to be my only occupation.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could offer #self.friend# the very worst spoon I've cut.
b : As a jest? | Would you sign it?
a : As a promise the next one will actually carry broth. | Yes, and send a clean cloth for the table.

scene home
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a peg whose elbow points the coat away from the wall.
b : Why away? | You've put thought into a peg.
a : Air can reach the fur while the coat rests. | Mostly the tree did. I just made the wise decision to stop cutting.

scene coin
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm suspicious when a price comes with more carving than the spoon.
b : Too fine for supper? | What's the part worth buying?
a : If I'm counting coins I'd like them to buy a bowl in the spoon. | A sound curve that won't leak the best of the gravy.

scene guest
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My advice to a newcomer is to find the cheapest wood spoon on the street.
b : For supper? | What does it show?
a : In due course. First see how much care went into a thing nobody boasts about. | Whether the maker thought of the wolf holding the handle.

scene sleep
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my sleep a cooking spoon once found my work wanting.
b : Did it speak? | What complaint?
a : It stood up in the bowl and wagged its handle till I woke. | It wanted a little more hollow where the soup ought to sit.

scene song
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dance best with a bit of elbow room and no tool in my belt.
b : What kind of step? | Afraid to lose the tool?
a : Less a step than an enthusiastic rearrangement of my feet. | Afraid of looking too official for a ridiculous dance.

scene health
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my thumb away from the line where a shaving wants to travel.
b : Does it help? | Is a shaving dangerous?
a : The thumb thinks so. It has never thanked me in writing. | No. The edge following behind is the less sociable part.

scene mix
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A damp stick bends politely and dries in a temper.
b : Can you count on it? | Temper in a stick?
a : I count on the grain. The weather has its own interests. | It'll twist away from the shape you were so proud of yesterday.

scene roadload
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A late wagon has a great many imaginary owners.
b : How so? | Who owns it really?
a : Every wolf waiting for a parcel feels personally entitled to move the wheels. | I wouldn't guess. I only know the owner can't pull it along by wishing.

story ladle [topic=memories]
  : I carved a spoon with a magnificent handle and entirely forgot to hollow out the bowl. It held about one generous drop.
  : I tried it in stew. The onion pieces sat on it well enough, but the broth turned round and made for home.
  b : Did you keep the spoon?
  : I called it an onion lifter. After a week I had the good sense to hollow it properly.

story stick [topic=travel]
  : I brought home a stick so pleasingly bent that I carried it round the long way to give it a debut. It fitted my hand like a cup handle.
  : At home I lifted it to the peg and found that my wrist wouldn't clear the little curl I liked so much.
  b : What became of your fine curl?
  : A handle for a small basket. The wood had a better idea than the walker.

story letter [topic=memories]
  : A drop of tea fell on the outside of a letter I'd kept safe a long time. I blotted it with a wood shaving before it could soak in.
  : The paper stayed clean, but the shaving took such a good stain I began admiring it and let my drink get cold.
  b : Was the letter all right?
  : Perfectly dry. Whatever else that letter has cost me, it hasn't yet cost a legible word.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=woodcutter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Leave the strong elbow on that limb. | The ladle judge would like a deeper cut.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=hard_cheese
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One more roof tile for my supper. | Cut the heel across its short side.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=long_walks
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a turn I've never given a whole afternoon. | A little distance for the sake of my own soles.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Fine light to find the natural bend. | No case heard till the shavings wake up.

dlg resident.hub : Come in on my unarmed side. The sharpest thing I have for visitors is generally an opinion.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I have another entirely uncalled-for opinion about ladles ready for you.
dlg resident.job [self.job=woodcutter self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. There's more than firewood in a good crooked branch.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This report had a fairly straight grain. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : Look for a spoon in the next tree you pass.

graft resident.hub
choice Who's this kitchen judge of yours? -> spoon_judge
node spoon_judge
say Any imaginary old cook with a suspicious eye for a shallow ladle. I can invent a crowd of grandmothers and not a single one will flatter me about my work.
free
choice What do those cooks say about a straight stick? -> spoon_stick
choice I'll try my luck with the ladle. -> hub
node spoon_stick
say Fine for a rolling pin. A terrible thing to waste on a bent spoon. You'll notice I allow the imaginary cook the better half of each argument.
choice I'll keep a straight stick for pastry. -> hub
choice I'd best leave the judges in peace. -> bye
